const slides = [{"title": "Sangam Gala", "text": "SANGAM gala\n\nISC × SLA × PA × NC × TELS × GS\n\nEnd-of-semester sit-down charity dinner.", "image": "assets/slide-01.jpg"}, {"title": "Cause", "text": "Our home of South Asia is a beautiful, vibrant place bustling with culture, and we are all proud to call it home. Just like anywhere, it also faces real challenges: women’s rights, educational opportunities, poverty and food security, human rights and press freedom, and many more.\n\nA charity dinner is a way to bring people together in support of a cause, creating an evening that offers more than a simple appeal for donations.", "image": "assets/slide-02.jpg"}, {"title": "Shortlist", "text": "Education\nAccess to education continues to be limited for many people living in South Asia. While literacy rates are improving, obstacles remain for those who are poor or live in rural areas.\n\nEnvironment / Climate\nNatural disasters devastate communities quickly. Funds could support immediate relief.\n\nWomen’s rights\nWomen still face unequal opportunities in areas such as employment and are disproportionately affected by domestic violence.\n\nThese are shortlisted causes; a beneficiary has not yet been selected.", "image": "assets/slide-03.jpg"}, {"title": "The evening", "text": "Where did “Sangam” come from?\nSangam is a Sanskrit-derived word meaning “union” or “coming together” — the same way our six societies are coming together for this night and a shared cause.\n\nProposed run sheet\nArrival & drinks\nWelcome & cause introduction\nDinner service\nPerformances\nDate auction\nDance floor opens\nClosing & total raised announced live", "image": "assets/slide-04.jpg"}, {"title": "Enchanted garden", "text": "Enchanted garden\n\nThe visual inspiration: deep green drapery, candlelit tables, botanical arrangements, hanging greenery, and warm gold details. These images are a mood board, not a confirmed venue.", "image": "assets/slide-05.jpg"}, {"title": "Format", "text": "A sit-down charity dinner, timed after exams as an end-of-semester party.\n\nThe proposal omits a bar tab because of its large expense.\n\nWhy a sit-down ball?\nThe societies already offer a busy calendar of stand-up events. This is an opportunity for a different kind of evening: dressing up, meaningful speeches, dinner, and a charity date auction.", "image": "assets/slide-06.jpg"}, {"title": "Date auction", "text": "A fully opt-in charity date auction\n\nParticipants offer a chaperoned lunch, with the highest bidder winning the opportunity to attend. No executive should feel pressured to participate. The proposal expects the bulk of donations to come from ticket sales.\n\nLunches would be chaperoned, with a restaurant booked for the group and organisers keeping tabs on participants’ wellbeing.\n\nAll contact goes through official channels and society pages. No phone numbers are shared unless the participant chooses to continue contact.", "image": "assets/slide-07.jpg"}, {"title": "An example", "text": "Sandes Welagedara\nTreasurer\n                 st\n    Degree:      1 Year Medicine\n   Ethnicity:    Sinhalese, Sri Lankan\nSpecial Skill:   Decent at cooking; can outdrink any Indian any day\n Green Flag:     Easy to talk to; pragmatic and optimistic\n   Red Flag:     Perfectionist; overly meticulous and particular\n       Prize: 1x chaperoned platonic lunch date at [restaurant]\n\n\n\nStarting Bid                 $20                                      PUNJABI ASSOCIATION", "image": "assets/slide-08.jpg"}, {"title": "Involvement", "text": "Why these six clubs?\nPA, GS, ISC, TELS, NC and SLA bring together South Asian communities at UQ. A shared cause means shared impact, shared reach, and a night that reflects how connected our communities already are.\n\nHow would costs be shared?\nUpfront costs would be split according to each society’s ability. All upfront society contributions would be reimbursed from gross ticket revenue before net proceeds are donated to charity.\n\nTicket profits are not split between societies. The intention is to cover costs and maximise the charitable donation.", "image": "assets/slide-09.jpg"}, {"title": "Interested?", "text": "Interested? Come talk to me.\n\nThe proposal suggests starting planning in Semester 2 and looking for venues that can seat 500 guests, provide competitively priced catering, and support a cause from the shortlist.\n\nA note on sponsors\nSocieties are invited to approach their current sponsors. Sponsor recognition could include a shoutout on the night and, for significant support, logos displayed on the screens.\n\nA new event for all of us.\n\nDates, venue, beneficiary and ticket details are still to be confirmed.", "image": "assets/slide-10.jpg"}, {"title": "Together", "text": "Welcome to SANGAM gala\n\nIn collaboration with our six societies.", "image": "assets/slide-11.jpg"}, {"title": "Sangam", "text": "Welcome to SANGAM gala\n\nComing together for a shared cause.", "image": "assets/slide-12.jpg"}];
